{
  "dom_id": "step-e4744",
  "name": "Example: Writing a Product of Two Square Roots as a Single Square Root",
  "problem": "Write $3 \\sqrt{5}$ as the square root of a single number.",
  "worked_solution": "Note that $3 = \\sqrt{9}.$ So, applying the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n3 \\sqrt{5} = \\sqrt{9}\\cdot\\sqrt{5}= \\sqrt{9\\cdot 5} = \\sqrt{45}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
